 ### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-
-*   **Captioning Efficacy:** Image captioning efficacy diminishes for images of lower quality or those with pronounced artifacts. Textual inversion is used to optimize a shared latent text embedding $s^*$ to counteract this [S1].
-*   **Noisy Data Augmentation:** When training the diffusion model with noisy RGB-depth data augmentation (where uncertainty maps are not available), uncertainty maps are not fed into the diffusion model [S1].
-*   **Precision:** The pixel transformation $q = K R_{B \rightarrow A} D_A(p) K^{-1} p$ requires accurate camera intrinsics $K$ and relative poses $R_{B \rightarrow A}$ to enforce epipolar constraints correctly [S1].
+*   **Captioning Efficacy:** Image captioning efficacy diminishes for low-quality images or those with pronounced artifacts. This is mitigated by optimizing the shared latent text embedding $s^*$ via textual inversion [S1].
+*   **Augmentation Data:** When training the diffusion model with noisy RGB-depth data augmentation (where uncertainty maps are not available), uncertainty maps are not fed into the diffusion model [S1].
+*   **Uncertainty Calculation:** The uncertainty map relies on the accuracy of the rendered depth $D_A$. If depth estimation is poor, the warping $I_{B \rightarrow A}$ may be inaccurate, leading to misleading uncertainty values [S1].
 
